The adapted material includes:
- PeriodicODE, FiniteVolume, and RotationWork: compact integral calculus,
  rotation geometry, probability invariance, and Gibbs/gauge/Ward patterns.
- MixedAlgebra, MixedWard, ComplexWard, FamilyKernel, FamilyBound,
  FamilyEstimate, FamilyLower, and RotationInequality: mixed fourth-order
  algebra and finite-family contraction patterns.
- Interaction-independent smooth-profile, lattice, dyadic-mode, Fourier
  operator, matrix-square, and annular response estimates: the corresponding
  subsections are marked in RP2/FourierAll.lean.
- PotentialRotation, PeriodicPartition, and AnnulusPartition: boundary
  rotation paths and the periodic partition-ratio argument.

Modifications include changed imports and namespaces; specialization to the
three-dimensional spin sphere; replacement of the linear edge interaction by
its square; new squared-interaction derivative jets and mixed coefficients;
new coefficient/current bounds; and explicit connection to the RP2 partition
function and pinned kernels. The pure Fourier construction is independent of
this interaction change.

RP2-specific additions include concrete tetrahedral rotations and cancellation,
exact integration and edge allocation for disjoint annular interiors, retained
lattice restrictions, uniform factorial and real-exponent bounds, an explicit
logarithmic envelope, and weak-limit/summability statements. Relevant source
files carry local provenance notes.

RP3 extension (October 2026)
---------------------------
The RP3 namespace adapts the RP2 version 0.4.0 proof to unit vectors in real
four-space, with quaternion half-generators and quaternion-unit averaging.
The original RP2 modules and their provenance remain unchanged. The lattice
Fourier and annular proofs are adapted in the RP3 namespace. See README-RP3.md
for the exact model, theorem scope, and verification instructions.

RP3 review revision (October 2026)
---------------------------------
The moment/positivity, compactness, and SO(3) bridge proofs integrate code in
the Claude Opus review supplied by the user as RP3-Improvement-Suggestions.lean.
The original review is retained under review/ and its scope is discussed in
REVIEW-RESPONSE.md. The RP3 high-temperature development adapts the supplied
RP2 version 0.4.0 active-edge and nonbacktracking path proofs.

